//? Title: SFC64: actual word/counter transitions and finite-prefix diagnostics
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Generate reproducible64-bit pseudorandom words from three state words and a
counter. Actual native snapshots show a hand-checkable step before the original
seed0xC0FFEE distribution calls and finite-prefix counts.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

All word arithmetic is modulo2^64. Output=a+b+counter, then increment the
counter; replace a by b xor (b right-shift11), b by9*c, and c by
rotate-left(c,24)+output. The local historical seed recipe uses three SplitMix64
words and counter1 without warmup; this differs from some external library
initialization recipes. A raw snapshot excludes the inherited normal spare;
copying the complete engine preserves it. Because the counter advances
modulo2^64, equality of complete states requires a multiple of2^64 steps, but
that observation alone does not specify the full output period or prove
randomness.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sfc64_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    namespace r = dm::random;
    r::Sfc64 engine(std::array<std::uint64_t, 4>{1, 2, 3, 4});
    auto s = engine.next_trace();
    std::print("Actual before `{}`, actual output {}, actual after `{}`.\n",
               s.before, s.value, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Raw a,b,c,counter = 1,2,3,4");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual output {}", s.value));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual next state {}", s.after));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/sfc64_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Actual before `[1, 2, 3, 4]`, actual output 7, actual after `[2, 27, 50331655, 5]`.
