> API and interpretation

Raw uint64 output is exact; displayed floating transforms depend on the common
sampler and host libm. Distribution calls consume different numbers of raw words
and may use a cached normal spare. The original sequence must be evaluated in
separate statements because C++ function-argument evaluation order is
unspecified. Prefix diagnostics do not prove independence, cryptographic
security or a complete period.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

